  "title": "Invention of the wheel",
  "summary": "Evidence indicates the wheel was created as a potter's wheel around 3500 BCE in Mesopotamia, some 300 years before it was used for chariots. By about 3000 BCE the Sumerians were using carts and wagons to move people and goods. The oldest wheel found so far, the Ljubljana Marshes Wheel, comes from Central Europe, though the idea is believed to have started earlier in Mesopotamia.",
